---
import Guide from '../layouts/Guide.astro';
import { links } from '../config/site';
---
<Guide
  title="Is There Government Burial Insurance?"
  h1="Is there government burial insurance?"
  description="There's no government burial insurance for the public. What Social Security and the VA really pay, and how to spot misleading 'burial benefit' ads."
  path="/government-burial-insurance/"
  crumb="Government burial insurance"
  eyebrow="Straight talk"
  lede="Short answer: no. If a mailer or ad says there's a state or federal program that pays for your funeral, it's selling private insurance."
  summary={[
    "There is no government burial insurance for the general public.",
    "Social Security pays a one-time $255 to an eligible surviving spouse or child, not to the funeral home.",
    "Eligible veterans may get a VA burial allowance and burial in a national cemetery.",
    "Ads that look official are private insurance. Check the insurer's name and the agent's license.",
  ]}
>
  <h2>What actually exists</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Social Security's $255 death payment.</strong> A one-time payment to an eligible surviving spouse or child, not to the funeral home.
      <a href={links.ssaDeath} rel="noopener">See ssa.gov</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>VA burial benefits for veterans.</strong> Eligible veterans may get a burial allowance and burial in a national cemetery.
      <a href={links.vaBurial} rel="noopener">See va.gov</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>VALife.</strong> The VA's own whole life insurance for veterans with a service-connected disability.
      <a href={links.valife} rel="noopener">About VALife</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>For most families these don't come close to covering a funeral, which is why private final expense insurance exists.</p>

  <h2>How to spot a misleading ad</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It says "state program," "government benefit," "state-regulated burial plan" or uses an official-looking seal.</li>
    <li>It says coverage is "free" or that you've "already qualified."</li>
    <li>It promises "guaranteed approval" without mentioning a waiting period.</li>
    <li>It doesn't name the insurance company or the licensed agent.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout callout--warn">
    <h3>What an honest agent does instead</h3>
    <p>
      Names the insurer, shows a license you can check, explains any waiting period, and never pressures you to decide on the first call.
      Our Florida license numbers are listed on every page of this site.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Where this leaves you</h2>
  <p>
    If you want a funeral paid for without leaving the bill to family, a small whole life policy is the usual answer.
    <a href="/final-expense-insurance-florida/">See how it works in Florida</a> or <a href="/final-expense-insurance-cost/">what it costs</a>.
  </p>
</Guide>
